{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1563851-your-opion-on-white-wolf-possibly-introducing-tribal-hauglosk-for-w6","id":1563851,"title":"Your Opion on White Wolf possibly introducing Tribal Hauglosk for W6.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-09-05T04:50:44-07:00","id":1563851,"title":"Your Opion on White Wolf possibly introducing Tribal Hauglosk for W6.","content":"So this post assumes many things. Among them the fact that white wolf would have most of the elements slated to be introduce in V6 to carry across all game lines consistently and the fact that there would be a W6 in the first place...<br /> <br /> Now since V6 has introduce Clan frenzes for I wonder if White wolf would revisit the concept of tribal Hauglosk that was somewhat experimented on in the Cancelled Hunter entertainment version of W5 as a post from JF Sambrano's <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/jfsambrano/posts/glass-walkers-97379727?utm_medium=clipboard_copy&amp;utm_source=copyLink&amp;utm_campaign=postshare_fan&amp;utm_content=web_share\" target=\"_blank\">parton </a>has shown:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Ghreena* of the Glass Walkers is the sterilization of the Wyld.<br /> <br /> The Glass Walkers flip the usual narrative of the Triat represented by Garou on its head, suggesting that the Wyld is at fault for driving the Weaver mad, which resulted in its machinations on the Wyrm. They will turn the tools of the Weaver on the Wyld with intent, building dams that provide &quot;clean energy&quot; while destroying ecosystems, genetically modifying crops to make them more durable against weather and pests, or creating low carbon footprint technologies which require mining operations that poison animals, people, and waterways. Many Glass Walkers favor terraforming the &quot;undesirable&quot; aspects of Gaia, such as deserts, by diverting waterways and creating solar panel fields which make these spaces more hospitable for humanity. They might claim that these actions are made out of a need for progress, but they seek out the sterilization of unstable qualities in the environment.<br /> <br /> *the cancelled edition term for hauglosk.\u200b </div> </div> </div>Like a glass walker under the influence of this version of Hauglosk would at best advocate for geoengineering project that could help the environment at the cost of bending it ever so subtly towards the weaver to draining out the local water table to cool they &quot;Carbon neutral&quot; LLM servers so that it MIGHT Develop into a AGI that figure out a way to seal away the Wrym for good. Which is frankly much more dynamic than how hauglosk was portrayed in W5.<br /> <br /> Not how the other tribes hauglosk could manifest, Like one idea I have sliver fang could go all Quixote, Usually not in the sense that they grow so detached from realty that they view warps into a fantasy novel, but they see themselves as the protagonist of they story and will fly into hysterics towards anything that contest it.<br /> <br /> I personally think this version of hauglosk implemented properly (tall ask I know) would be a upgrade to W5 verson (but well low bar and all..). Especially in conjunction with the V6 Forsaken 2e inspired humanity bar.<br /> <br /> What are your thoughts on this topic?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-07T07:54:53-07:00","id":1563893,"title":"","content":"Frankly, I'm surprised something like Hauglosk wasn't already in the game from the start.<br /> <br /> Garou are pretty much iconic for being rage fueled killing machines.<br /> <br /> With shit like the <b>Impergium</b> and <b>War of Rage</b> on their resume, you would think a condition that causes them to mentally snap and succumb to zealotry would be more common.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-07T17:55:35-07:00","id":1563905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1563851-your-opion-on-white-wolf-possibly-introducing-tribal-hauglosk-for-w6?p=1563893#post1563893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frankly, I'm surprised something like Hauglosk wasn't already in the game from the start.<br /> <br /> Garou are pretty much iconic for being rage fueled killing machines.<br /> <br /> With shit like the <b>Impergium</b> and <b>War of Rage</b> on their resume, you would think a condition that causes them to mentally snap and succumb to zealotry would be more common.</div> </div> </div> </div>Moreover, the 90s liked heavy-handed &quot;the GM controls your character here, you filthy cheating player!&quot; setups, an White Wolf in particular.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-08T02:41:49-07:00","id":1563909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1563851-your-opion-on-white-wolf-possibly-introducing-tribal-hauglosk-for-w6?p=1563893#post1563893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frankly, I'm surprised something like Hauglosk wasn't already in the game from the start.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was, was called status quo.<br /> <br /> Hauglosk pairs with Harano. The point of the game was that one of the unspoken reasons the Nation was loosing was because they had too many influential elders who were violent assholes trying to solve all their macroscale problems with indiscriminate brutality.<br /> <br /> So if one extreme is a Garou losing because of emotional exhaustion impairing them, the other is losing because satisfaction took precedence over complex approaches.<br /> <br /> The twist is that this was the actual cause of the loss, or one of the main causes. Which is also the reason why hope was real: changing their society is a daunting task, but is doable if only barely, and they can in fact change the tide of the war if they manage this.<br /> <br /> What W5 did, other than totally misunderstand the actual dynamics and purpose of Harano and Rage in Werewolf, was to name something the game always had and already worked.<br /> <br /> Now, do I think the balance scale for them can be salvaged in a new and interesting mechanic for the game? Yes. But it isn't strictly necessary and the game had the concept in place at least since 2nd Edition.<br /> <br /> And not having a name for Hauglosk was kind of the point: the problem was dire because the Elders didn't recognized it existed in the first place. That social reform in the Nation was not a distraction, but a necessity. In W5 what you call Hauglosk the Cult of Fenris calls common sense, and that's the situation in Legacy, just not stupidly written.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-23T13:19:37-07:00","id":1564308,"title":"","content":"I do think that introducing the term makes perfect sense as a way to indicate that the Garou Nation has made at least some progress towards comprehending an age-old problem (Thoigh probably not towards handling it).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}